WEBVTT

00:00:11.198 --> 00:00:13.557
I don't mean
to be indelicate here,

00:00:13.718 --> 00:00:16.798
but someone should get some ice,
keep the body fresh.

00:00:20.088 --> 00:00:22.147
He's just a silly little alien.

00:00:22.927 --> 00:00:23.967
He didn't belong here!

00:00:26.048 --> 00:00:27.388
That little alien

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:31.768
knew more about being human
than you ever will.

00:00:32.867 --> 00:00:33.867
His name was Sonic.

00:00:34.987 --> 00:00:36.027
This was his home.

00:00:37.508 --> 00:00:38.508
And he was my friend.

00:00:39.267 --> 00:00:41.818
[electricity crackling]

00:01:03.647 --> 00:01:04.807
He's all yours.

00:01:06.527 --> 00:01:07.668
[Tom]
Everyone, get back!

00:01:11.397 --> 00:01:14.177
I think you have something
that belongs to me.

00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:16.099
Whoa.

00:01:18.058 --> 00:01:20.307
[powering down]

00:01:25.458 --> 00:01:27.098
This is my power.

00:01:27.358 --> 00:01:29.498
And I'm not using it
to run away anymore.

00:01:30.098 --> 00:01:33.178
I'm using it
to protect my friends.

00:01:37.378 --> 00:01:39.799
[weapons powering up]

00:01:47.062 --> 00:01:49.874
[whirring]

00:01:56.710 --> 00:01:58.454
[beeping]

00:02:02.583 --> 00:02:04.151
[launching]

00:02:17.359 --> 00:02:18.462
[grunts]

00:02:30.282 --> 00:02:31.919
[exclaiming]
[alarms blaring]

00:02:32.027 --> 00:02:33.127
Ooh! Now you've done it!

00:02:33.288 --> 00:02:34.328
Guess what, Eggman?

00:02:34.608 --> 00:02:37.047
I'm not leaving Earth. You are.

00:02:37.727 --> 00:02:38.727
Donut Lord?

00:03:12.043 --> 00:03:14.500
[Robotnik yells]

00:03:23.391 --> 00:03:25.778
[people cheering, clapping]

00:03:27.647 --> 00:03:30.467
I told you, you got this.
Hey, wegot this.

00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:33.850
[gasps]

00:03:34.286 --> 00:03:35.626
[laughing]

00:03:42.897 --> 00:03:45.418
I think these belong to you.
Thank you very much.

00:03:46.958 --> 00:03:48.557
No more pushing people
off of buildings.

00:03:48.977 --> 00:03:50.217
You know
I can't promise that.

00:03:53.397 --> 00:03:56.537
You did pretty good, space hog.
Thanks, Donut Lord.

00:03:56.877 --> 00:03:59.937
You're gonna have to explain
this "Donut Lord" thing.

00:04:00.037 --> 00:04:02.697
Nope, sorry. That's for me
and the little guy. Right?

00:04:02.697 --> 00:04:06.137
We got our thing, you got
your thing with your... sister.
Oh, my God, my sister.

00:04:06.358 --> 00:04:10.118
Gotta go fast. Gotta go fast.
Gotta go fast. Gotta go fast.

00:04:11.057 --> 00:04:12.337
Jojo, put on my Fitbit...

00:04:13.697 --> 00:04:15.217
so I can at least
get some steps.

00:04:15.657 --> 00:04:16.797
We can never go back there.

00:04:18.317 --> 00:04:19.317
I mean, are we?

00:04:21.697 --> 00:04:23.657
'Cause it kind of feels like
we're home right now.

00:04:25.077 --> 00:04:26.077
Really?

00:04:27.578 --> 00:04:30.738
I kind of feel like
I checked the "save a life" box

00:04:30.738 --> 00:04:31.738
off my bucket list.

00:04:34.553 --> 00:04:36.941
Now all I want to do
is spend my life

00:04:37.058 --> 00:04:38.077
with the people
I care about.

00:04:40.058 --> 00:04:41.077
I want to check that box.

00:04:42.617 --> 00:04:43.737
Okay, I like that.

00:04:44.758 --> 00:04:46.978
All right, everybody.
Nothing to see here.

00:04:47.638 --> 00:04:48.638
Let's disperse.

00:04:48.638 --> 00:04:50.478
Just another ordinary day
in Green Hills.

00:04:50.617 --> 00:04:52.117
Carl,
I'll take that chain saw.

00:04:52.798 --> 00:04:53.798
[Wade] Come on. Let's go!

00:04:54.838 --> 00:04:56.438
You act like
you've never seen a fight

00:04:56.438 --> 00:05:00.898
between
an intergalactic space rodent
and a robot with a doctorate.

00:05:09.837 --> 00:05:10.857
You got enough there?

00:05:11.777 --> 00:05:13.897
Yes, Mr. Manager.
Need any more?

00:05:13.977 --> 00:05:14.977
You get that away.

00:05:18.615 --> 00:05:20.123
[knock on door]

00:05:26.078 --> 00:05:27.418
Mr. and Mrs. Wachowski?

00:05:28.418 --> 00:05:29.418
Yes?

00:05:31.647 --> 00:05:33.987
A token of appreciation
from your government,

00:05:33.988 --> 00:05:37.007
for keeping quiet
about recent incidents,
which never occurred.

00:05:38.291 --> 00:05:39.360
[both laugh]

00:05:39.938 --> 00:05:40.938
[Tom] Wow!

00:05:41.317 --> 00:05:43.697
Wonder what it is.
Money to fix the house?

00:05:44.298 --> 00:05:46.397
Letter from the President?
You'll see.

00:05:46.958 --> 00:05:47.958
Okay.

00:05:51.317 --> 00:05:53.437
Olive Garden.
[Tom] Hmm, yeah.

00:05:53.557 --> 00:05:55.978
[chuckles]
The way you said "You'll see"
made me think

00:05:55.978 --> 00:05:57.757
it was something better
than the things we said.

00:05:57.857 --> 00:05:59.557
Have you tried their
Never Ending Pasta Bowl?

00:06:00.517 --> 00:06:01.777
It never ends.
[Maddie chuckles]

00:06:01.882 --> 00:06:04.112
That sounds... fancy.
Mm-hmm. Mm-hmm.

00:06:04.217 --> 00:06:06.677
Well, thank you.
We appreciate the gesture.

00:06:07.737 --> 00:06:10.337
Oh, hey. I guess
we can close the file
on that Robotnik guy, huh?

00:06:10.937 --> 00:06:11.937
Just disappeared.

00:06:12.078 --> 00:06:13.078
I'm sorry,

00:06:13.097 --> 00:06:16.257
but no such person exists
or ever has existed.

00:06:17.637 --> 00:06:18.657
I wish that were true.

00:06:18.657 --> 00:06:20.697
You haven't by any chance
been in contact

00:06:20.697 --> 00:06:23.437
with a certain alien creature
since the incident, have you?

00:06:23.778 --> 00:06:25.438
Uncle Sam would love
to have a chat with him.

00:06:25.578 --> 00:06:27.858
Very casual.
Brunch, perhaps.

00:06:29.757 --> 00:06:31.097
Oh, you mean
the little blue guy.

00:06:31.097 --> 00:06:32.097
Mmm.No.

00:06:32.132 --> 00:06:33.982
No, nothing. No.
Mm-mmm.

00:06:34.077 --> 00:06:36.377
Doubt we'll ever
hear from him again.
Mm-mmm.

00:06:37.357 --> 00:06:38.357
Very well.

00:06:38.937 --> 00:06:39.937
Okay.

00:06:40.237 --> 00:06:42.477
Thank you.
Great.

00:06:42.575 --> 00:06:43.625
Mmm.

00:06:44.279 --> 00:06:45.266
Yep.

00:06:45.266 --> 00:06:48.449
[door creaks]

00:06:48.548 --> 00:06:50.928
To be honest, I'm pretty
pumped about the pasta bowl.

00:06:50.928 --> 00:06:51.928
[chuckles]

00:06:51.928 --> 00:06:53.768
So, do you guys wanna
watch a movie or what?

00:06:54.008 --> 00:06:55.348
Sorry, buddy,
it's a school night.

00:06:55.488 --> 00:06:56.948
It's time for you
to go back to your cave.

00:06:57.208 --> 00:06:58.907
What?
It's 3:00 in the afternoon!

00:06:59.168 --> 00:07:00.608
You know how you get
when you're tired. Come on.

00:07:00.748 --> 00:07:02.048
Me? I'm not like anything.

00:07:02.428 --> 00:07:05.588
[groans] You guys are so uncool.
Yeah, yeah, we know.

00:07:05.787 --> 00:07:07.348
[groans]
Hey, buddy, where you going?

00:07:07.527 --> 00:07:09.108
You said I have to
go back to my cave.

00:07:09.808 --> 00:07:10.808
We did.

